# kin/youth/arms/arm_r: the youth's right arm: a 3-row sleeve, the cuff row, a 3 x 2 hand (regions: U upper arm, C cuff, H hand)
# KIN-YOUTH (P2b wave 2). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. The sleeve is drawn in cloth1 (a long sleeve); the regions let a
# garment show a puff sleeve (dress: U linen, C skin), rolled sleeves, a trimmed cuff (coat, robe: C accent) or bare arms.
# Front and back: the forward swing comes toward the camera (the hand a row lower in front, higher from behind), the
# back swing away. Side views: the arm swings from the shoulder in whole-pixel steps, the hand ahead or behind the hip;
# runF the forearm bent up and forward, runB the arm driven back. `back` (left view) is the far hand peeking past the
# hip on the back swing.
use person
body youth
role arms std
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys armR
side R

view D key idle origin 1 -1
mark handR 0 3
|597
